    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's what I implemented.\n\n## Change: owner identity redesign\n\nThe `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>` and the sequence number is gone. Every value derived from the code follows automatically.\n\n**New shared utility \u2014 `Sha256`**\nExtracted the SHA-256-to-hex logic (previously private in `HouseholdIdGenerator`) into `util/Sha256.hex(String)`. `HouseholdIdGenerator` now reuses it instead of holding its own copy \u2014 no duplicated crypto code.\n\n**`CustomerCodeGenerator` (redesigned)**\n- `format(region, normalizedTelephone, lastName)` \u2192 `region + \"-\" + HASH8`, where `HASH8` is the first 8 upper-case hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)`.\n- `region(customerCode)` \u2192 extracts the `REGION` prefix, so the code is the single home for both building and parsing the identity.\n- Dropped the old city/last-name/sequence formatting entirely.\n\n**`ClinicServiceImpl.createOwner`**\nBuilds the code from the new identity: `CustomerCodeGenerator.format(LocalityResolver.resolve(city, postcode), owner.getTelephone(), owner.getLastName())`. The telephone is already E.164-normalized by the mapper before the service runs. `countByCity` stays \u2014 it still enforces the per-city capacity cap; it just no longer feeds a sequence.\n\n**Locality moved onto the identity**\n- Added `LocalityResolver.fromCustomerCode(customerCode, city, postcode)`, which reads the region from the `customerCode` and falls back to the existing `resolve(...)` for owners with no code (seed data), keeping their locality unchanged.\n- `OwnerMapper` now derives `locality` from the customer code.\n\n**Automatically follow (consume `customerCode` verbatim):** membership number, Luhn check digit, and the create audit record \u2014 the audit line now logs `customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`.\n\n**Docs:** updated the stale `OwnerRepository.countByCity` Javadoc (it referenced the removed sequence).\n\nAll tests pass (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`), including the acceptance check that `customerCode` matches `[A-Z0-9]+-[0-9A-F]{8}`.",
